---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { rel, SUPPORT_EMAIL, LEGAL_NAME } from '../../consts';
const description = `Privacy policy for TaxShelf by ${LEGAL_NAME}.`;
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy · TaxShelf" description={description} path="/privacy/taxshelf">
  <main class="page">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:720px;">
      <a class="back" href={rel('/privacy/')}>← All privacy policies</a>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">TaxShelf · Last updated September 25, 2026</p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        TaxShelf keeps the tax documents you choose to record, one shelf per tax year: the document type, a label,
        an amount if you type one, notes, and an optional photo or PDF. It shows a countdown to the file-by date you
        pick. Your shelf stays on your iPhone unless you turn on AI assistants. The app has no ads and no tracking.
        TaxShelf is not a tax filing service and does not give tax advice.
      </p>

      <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Every tax year, document, amount, note, and attachment you add.</li>
        <li>Attachments (photos and PDFs) never leave your iPhone, even with AI assistants turned on.</li>
        <li>If you turn on AI assistants, a random account ID and a device key kept in the iOS Keychain.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If you never turn on AI assistants, {LEGAL_NAME} receives nothing. Deleting the app removes all of it.</p>

      <h2>If you turn on AI assistants (optional)</h2>
      <p>
        Under Settings → AI assistants you can connect an assistant such as Claude so it can read your shelf. There
        is no sign-in: the app creates a random account with no name, email, or phone number. After you connect:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          your saved shelf (tax years, file-by dates, and the document fields you typed, with attachment file names
          but not the files) is copied to TaxShelf's server at taxshelf.dudleyapps.com, encrypted at rest, and
          reachable only by your account;
        </li>
        <li>
          an assistant you link with a one-time code from the app can read that shelf. It can never add, change, or
          delete anything. The full export pack for a year works only while you grant it in the app;
        </li>
        <li>
          we use this data only to provide the connection. We don't sell it, share it for advertising, or use it to
          train models.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Revoke any assistant in the app at any time. <strong>Turn off and delete server copy</strong> removes the
        server copy and disconnects every assistant immediately; your shelf on your iPhone stays. What an assistant
        does with the information it reads is governed by that assistant's own privacy policy.
      </p>

      <h2>Reminders</h2>
      <p>
        File-by reminders are local notifications scheduled on your iPhone, and only if you allow notifications. No
        push server is involved.
      </p>

      <h2>Purchases</h2>
      <p>
        TaxShelf Pro, a one-time purchase, unlocks other tax years, unlimited documents, and export packs. Apple
        processes payment through StoreKit; we never see your payment details. Purchases can be restored from
        Settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Used to track you</h2>
      <p>Nothing. TaxShelf has no advertising or analytics SDKs, and we do not sell personal data.</p>

      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>The server copy is kept until you delete it in the app. We also delete it on request by email.</p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>TaxShelf is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal data from them.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes materially, the new version will be posted at this URL with an updated date above.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions or a deletion request? Email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
